Z||000022||FieroSEt||05-27-2001||06:44 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Loki:<BR><B>Hey, what problems might incure if panels need to be removed? Did you make it so they can? Ir they on for good?  Like the door panels and such...<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey Loki....  What's up???  How's Big D??  <BR>Well as far as removing any panel's oranything will ...lol  probably have to be cut out...  and then re~done.  I can't really see a way to make them seamless AND removable...       I hope all this work is'nt for nothing...  I just hope that it does'nt REALLY look MR2'sh...  Does it??  <BR>Well...  No one can really tell how it's going to look ...  We will after I glass in the sail~scoop's tho...  he he <BR> Stay safe and I plan to make a N*Texas Fiero's meeting when I'm finished completly. I also want to make a meeting in Oklahoma ..  up there with the other fiberglass idiot...   momo..     Behave Loki...   lol          Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka... 1FieroGTRacingInc.<BR>Tyler,Texas<BR>Fiero_87GT@Yahoo.com<BR>(903)445-0849  cell phone||||reg||1
Z||000023||Philphine||05-27-2001||07:41 PM||||how are you working out the side marker lights? i'll need to work out some kind of smooth facias myself. <P>also, i've used some stuff called 3m auto mix urethane bumper repair to fill in the seam at the bottom of the facia. you know, where it looks like ground effects have been added to a regular facia. haven't sanded it down yet but it's been on there awhile and it seems to flex with the bumper really well. kinda costly though.||||reg||1
