Z||000025||FieroSEt||05-28-2001||01:13 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Philphine:<BR><B>how are you working out the side marker lights? i'll need to work out some kind of smooth facias myself. <P>also, i've used some stuff called 3m auto mix urethane bumper repair to fill in the seam at the bottom of the facia. you know, where it looks like ground effects have been added to a regular facia. haven't sanded it down yet but it's been on there awhile and it seems to flex with the bumper really well. kinda costly though.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I'm planning on cutting and inserting a set just below the level of the orinal's, behind rear tire and infront of the front tire.. of course..  I'm not sure on what set as of yet, though, I can access from the underneath, and from outside for the installation...  any suggestion's on a great looking set that would fit the Fiero...<P>I'll look into that 3M product, thank's...  <BR>                              Steve<P>------------------<BR>aka... 1FieroGTRacingInc.<BR>Tyler,Texas<BR>Fiero_87GT@Yahoo.com<BR>(903)445-0849  cell phone||||reg||1
